# Files that come from the skeleton base repo, checked by .claude/hooks/protect-base.sh in
# project repos (any repo with a `base` git remote). The skeleton itself is never blocked.
#
#   locked <pattern>  Claude may not edit it. Generic changes go to the skeleton; project
#                     needs are built in project-owned code around it.
#   shared <pattern>  An extension point projects are expected to change. Claude must keep
#                     the change additive and project-specific, and the user confirms each edit.
#
# Patterns are bash globs relative to the repo root; `*` also matches `/`, so `dir/*` covers
# everything under dir. A user can allow a locked path in one project by listing it in
# .claude/base-overrides (which only the user edits).

